# Single-Repo vs Workspace Setup

## Rule

- **Single-repo work** (agent in one repo, local dev in one repo): Run `bash scripts/setup.sh` in that repo only.
- **Workspace-wide changes** (deps changed, pushing to main): Follow `codex/08-workflows/ci-cd-flow.md` — version alignment → run-all-setup → sync-to-main.

## When to Use Each

| Context | Command | Why |
|---------|---------|-----|
| Agent working in execution-service | `cd execution-service && bash scripts/setup.sh` | That repo only; no workspace-wide ops |
| You changed pyproject.toml in 3 repos | `run-version-alignment.sh --fix` then `run-all-setup.sh` | Workspace-wide alignment + uv.lock refresh |
| Pushing local changes to main | `sync-all-to-main.sh` | Full flow (after alignment + setup if deps changed) |

